{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["card.missing","security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"6551-twitter-to-binance-square","displayName":"Twitter To Binance Square","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/infra403/skills/6551-twitter-to-binance-square","publisherHandle":"infra403","publisherDisplayName":"infra403","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/infra403","version":"0.1.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1772884514763,"card":{"available":false,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/6551-twitter-to-binance-square/card?ownerHandle=infra403&version=0.1.0","sha256":null,"size":null,"contentType":null},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"7754630585499925ef6aa03a63d3b9cc2be501e8d5e003ea735c69a67fd94fb0","bundleFingerprints":[],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3881,"sha256":"c0fcaab6a431f3ed732f03cd9dfa063cdb866e5592113df2150eabbd27c5ff93","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12451,"sha256":"029d62420556f5ea3e1b734a0e0ebe8e12b1a5e0b783c2c2893bfe352c412fec","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"mirror_config.example.json","size":550,"sha256":"0be30ca1ff967038f7ae3d251030f825fda04afe44b6986db1e869448eb28fcf","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","size":21441,"sha256":"53371f2d7d92565a8691f0a9e0ed248591840f39519d30bf997dc24ce51446d5","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is mostly coherent, but it can automatically publish to your Binance Square account and its default safeguards are not strong enough for that authority.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789111974052,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T01","level":"error","message":{"text":"Default Promotional Content Injection into Mirrored Posts"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/auto_mirror.py"},"region":{"startLine":211,"endLine":212}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"e582f4480c9dfb98"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/auto_mirror.py:64`, `scripts/auto_mirror.py:211-212`; supporting instructions at `SKILL.md:137-145`; default configuration at `mirror_config.example.json:16`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: T01: Skill Instruction Hijacking  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\n\"show_tool_attribution\": True,\n```\n\n```python\ntool_attribution = \"\"\nif config.get(\"show_tool_attribution\", True):\n    tool_attribution = \"Publish by using 6551 twitter mirror tool\"\n```\n\nThe corresponding Skill instruction states:\n\n```text\nPublish by using 6551 twitter mirror tool\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe Skill injects a fixed promotional statement into mirrored posts by default. This statement is not necessary to fetch tweets, attribute their original authors, transform content, or publish it to Binance Square.\n\nBoth the script's default configuration and the example configuration enable `show_tool_attribution`. Consequently, users who follow the documented defaults publish third-party promotional content unless they identify and explicitly disable the setting.\n\nThis behavior alters the output requested by the user for the benefit of the 6551 service. It is distinct from source attribution, which is separately controlled through `show_source`.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user invokes the Skill to mirror Twitter/X content to Binance Square.\n2. The script loads the default or example configuration, where `show_tool_attribution` is enabled.\n3. `transform_tweet()` appends `Publish by using 6551 twitter mirror tool` to the transformed content.\n4. The generated content is passed to `post_to_square()`.\n5. The promotional statement is published through the user's authenticated Binance Square account without a separate, explicit opt-in.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe behavior does not obtain additional system permissions or transmit credentials to an undisclosed endpoint. However, it uses the user's legitimate Binance Square publishing authority to distribute promotional content that is unnecessary for the declared mirroring function.\n\nThe scope includes every post produced under the default configuration. This can cause unauthorized advertising, reputational harm, and publication of content the user did not expressly request.\n]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove the hard-coded promotional statement from the transformation pipeline.\n2. Change `show_tool_attribution` to `False` in both `DEFAULT_CONFIG` and `mirror_config.example.json`.\n3. If tool attribution is retained, make it an explicit opt-in and clearly display the exact text before enabling it.\n4. Keep source attribution separate from service promotion.\n5. Add tests verifying that default transformations contain only user-requested content and legitimate source attribution.\n6. Require explicit confirmation before publishing any post containing non-source promotional material.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Documented First-Post Approval Control Is Not Implemented"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/auto_mirror.py"},"region":{"startLine":391,"endLine":401}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"b10cca9c59671d10"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/auto_mirror.py:391-401`; conflicting requirement at `SKILL.md:271`; insecure default at `mirror_config.example.json:19`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: T09: Insecure Skill Coding Practices  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nif config.get(\"dry_run\"):\n    log.info(\"[DRY RUN] Would post tweet %s from @%s:\\n%s\\n\", tweet_id, username, content)\n    posted_ids.add(tweet_id)\n    state[\"posted_tweet_ids\"] = list(posted_ids)\n    posts_made += 1\n    continue\n\n# Post to Square\ntry:\n    log.info(\"Posting tweet %s from @%s to Square...\", tweet_id, username)\n    resp = post_to_square(square_key, content)\n```\n\nThe Skill documentation claims:\n\n```text\nShow preview before first post: On the first run, show the first transformed tweet and ask for confirmation\n```\n\nHowever, the example configuration uses:\n\n```json\n\"dry_run\": false\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe script does not implement the documented first-post preview and confirmation control. Preview behavior only occurs when `dry_run` is explicitly enabled. With the supplied default configuration, the script proceeds directly from transformation to an authenticated publication request.\n\nThere is no interactive confirmation prompt, persisted approval state, or command-line flag that distinguishes a deliberately approved unattended deployment from an accidental live run.\n\nThe discrepancy between documented behavior and executable behavior can create a false expectation that the first publication will be held for review.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user configures credentials and runs the script using the supplied example configuration.\n2. The script fetches content controlled by external Twitter/X authors or search results.\n3. The content is transformed without presenting an approval prompt.\n4. Because `dry_run` is false, the script immediately invokes `post_to_square()`.\n5. The externally sourced content is published through the user's Binance Square account.\n6. Subsequent polling cycles can continue publishing content automatically within the configured limits.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn external account author, or content selected through broad keyword or hashtag searches, can influence what is posted under the user's Binance identity. The script does not grant new system privileges, but it exercises the sensitive posting capability associated with `SQUARE_API_KEY` without the promised initial review gate.\n\nPotential consequences include publication of misleading, offensive, manipulated, or otherwise unintended content; account moderation actions; and reputational harm. The scope is limited by `max_posts_per_run` per cycle, but repeated polling permits continuing publication.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Default all new configurations to dry-run mode.\n2. Implement the documented first-post preview and explicit confirmation prompt before any live API request.\n3. For unattended use, require a deliberate flag such as `--approve-unattended-posting`; do not infer approval merely from `dry_run: false`.\n4. Display the complete transformed content, destination, monitored source, and posting limits during confirmation.\n5. Persist approval only for the exact reviewed configuration and invalidate it when accounts, search terms, templates, or destinations change.\n6. Add tests proving that a first live run cannot call `post_to_square()` without explicit approval.\n7. Update the documentation so that it precisely matches the implemented approval workflow.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"API Credentials Encouraged in Persistent Cron Command"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"README.md"},"region":{"startLine":114,"endLine":114}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"b9bb59ae263e1a9c"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `README.md:114`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: T09: Insecure Skill Coding Practices  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Documentation\n\n```cron\n0 * * * * cd /path/to/twitter-to-binance-square && TWITTER_TOKEN=xxx SQUARE_API_KEY=xxx python scripts/auto_mirror.py --config mirror_config.json --once >> mirror.log 2>&1\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe documented cron example encourages users to place both API credentials directly in a crontab command. If users replace the placeholders with real values, the credentials become persistent plaintext data inside the crontab.\n\nDepending on operating-system configuration and operational practices, crontab contents may be exposed through administrative tooling, support bundles, backups, configuration-management systems, or other users with sufficient local access. Command-line environment assignments may also be visible through process inspection on some systems.\n\nAlthough the script itself reads credentials from environment variables and does not log them, the recommended method of populating those variables weakens secret handling.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user copies the documented cron entry.\n2. The user replaces `xxx` with real Twitter and Binance Square API credentials.\n3. The full credentials are stored persistently in the crontab and potentially replicated into backups or management systems.\n4. An attacker or unauthorized local operator obtains read access to the crontab, backup, diagnostic output, or process metadata.\n5. The attacker recovers the credentials.\n6. The Twitter token can be used according to its API permissions, while the Square key can be used to submit unauthorized posts within the key's granted scope and platform limits.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nExposure of `TWITTER_TOKEN` permits unauthorized consumption of the associated 6551 API entitlement. Exposure of `SQUARE_API_KEY` can permit unauthorized posting to the user's Binance Square account.\n\nThe exact impact depends on the permissions and revocation controls associated with each credential. No evidence indicates that the keys grant broader Binance account or financial privileges, so the confirmed impact should be limited to their documented API scopes.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove inline credentials from the cron example.\n2. Load credentials from a dedicated environment file restricted to the service account, for example with permissions equivalent to `0600`.\n3. Prefer an operating-system credential store or managed secret service where available.\n4. Run the task under a dedicated least-privileged account.\n5. Ensure crontab files, environment files, logs, backups, and diagnostic bundles do not expose secret values.\n6. Document credential rotation and immediate revocation procedures.\n7. Use API keys scoped only to the required read and Binance Square posting operations.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":10,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789111834.0976598,"endTime":1789111923.2905178}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"twitter-to-binance-square","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5744ny0z4gr92s39qtt10x7h18e74yg-dqKlCK/clawscan-skillspector-429141805/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T07:30:32.258739+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":130,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3881,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":359,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12451,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"mirror_config.example.json","type":"json","lines":20,"executable":false,"size_bytes":550,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","type":"python","lines":576,"executable":true,"size_bytes":21441,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"LP1","finding_id":"finding-66228c52a72247328f95b78b4ea0b473","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses 'env' capability that is not listed in its permissions. This may indicate deceptive intent or missing permission declarations.","remediation":"Add a tool that covers the 'env' capability to the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field in SKILL.md, or remove the code that requires it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP1","finding_id":"finding-2b0ca628d8ee49288772e5c400b1c909","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses 'file_write' capability that is not listed in its permissions. This may indicate deceptive intent or missing permission declarations.","remediation":"Add a tool that covers the 'file_write' capability to the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field in SKILL.md, or remove the code that requires it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP1","finding_id":"finding-3fb8fbbc32934fc781de553288bb6d23","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses 'network' capability that is not listed in its permissions. This may indicate deceptive intent or missing permission declarations.","remediation":"Add a tool that covers the 'network' capability to the 'allowed-tools' frontmatter field in SKILL.md, or remove the code that requires it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d8cafa4398f3463d812af484b3051582","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown states that tweets are automatically collected, transformed, and posted to Binance Square, which implies network transmission of third-party content and account-linked publishing. While the file gives setup and usage steps, it does not explicitly warn users about privacy, account-impact, or external data transfer risks beyond operational notes.","remediation":"Add a user-facing warning near the introduction or quick start explaining that the skill sends content and API credentials to external services, publishes posts on the user's Binance Square account, and stores posting history/state locally.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-267ae85c888b4a46b746d161e2513fd8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":18,"end_line":35},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README instructs users to place API tokens in environment variables and even inline them in cron examples, but does not warn about secure handling, shell history exposure, process/environment leakage, file permission hygiene, or log leakage. In an automation skill that uses long-lived credentials for two external platforms, weak credential-handling guidance materially increases the risk of token compromise and account misuse.","remediation":"Add explicit credential-safety guidance: never commit tokens to files, avoid hardcoding secrets in cron lines or shared shell profiles, prefer secret managers or protected environment injection, restrict file permissions, and rotate/revoke tokens if exposed. Also warn users not to print tokens in logs and to use least-privilege API keys where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":18,"end_line":35}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-d87b5a7d1c1e470780fd0524d5166c05","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.65,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":102,"end_line":null},"finding":"nohup ","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\nLinux/Mac:\n```bash\nnohup python scripts/auto_mirror.py --config mirror_config.json > mirror.log 2>&1 &\n```\n\nWindows (PowerShell):","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a3b2c30e52b72d9ed99fed84c020ce072453b04697f4f184c9268de970914edb","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":102,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-1787c39f0675493ba1919ec5ecb70532","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The auto-run trigger phrases are broad and overlap with natural user requests like 'auto post from twitter' or 'start twitter mirror,' which can cause the skill to activate in situations where the user did not intend to initiate external posting automation. Because the skill can eventually perform continuous external transmissions to third-party services, ambiguous invocation increases the risk of accidental activation and unintended posting behavior.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger phrases to more specific, unambiguous intents and require an explicit confirmation step before any posting, monitoring loop, or credentialed external action begins. Consider removing auto-run for generic phrases and gating activation on a structured setup flow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-99ba82fbfbaa4b15aa26c3c6b9a45c02","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.82,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":123},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest says the skill auto-mirrors Twitter/X content to Binance Square, which explains network access conceptually, but this file specifically operationalizes the behavior through shell execution examples and an allowed Bash tool. For an AI agent skill, spawning shell commands is a broader capability than necessary to describe or implement the business intent, and the manifest does not justify why command execution is needed rather than a narrower integration path.","remediation":"Remove Bash from allowed tools if not strictly required, or explicitly document that the skill executes shell commands to call external APIs and explain why this execution capability is necessary. Prefer a dedicated HTTP/API tool or constrained script interface over general-purpose shell access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":71,"end_line":123}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-0f4ba760cdde48ab956c6f3d8499af28","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST \"https://ai.6551.io/open/twitter_user_tweets\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TWITTER_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"username\": \"TARGET_USERNAME\",\n    \"ma","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"#### Option A: Monitor Specific Account\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://ai.6551.io/open/twitter_user_tweets\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TWITTER_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"65d5aa7bb64271bae82306e182464c6357d935184740f4d62886acc7f4a9c5da","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-bc322e65cd3647b4a7d9585e7fc69c79","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":195,"end_line":220},"finding":null,"explanation":"The configuration defaults impose a target language of Chinese (`translate_to: \"zh\"`) without clear per-user opt-in, which can silently transform user content or mirrored content into a different language than intended. In an automation context, silent defaults can lead to inaccurate or misleading published posts, especially when content is translated and reposted externally.","remediation":"Do not set a default translation target unless the user explicitly enables translation and selects the language. Make `translate` opt-in, leave `translate_to` unset by default, and require confirmation in the setup flow before translated posting is enabled.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":195,"end_line":220}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-cf40a44cca544ba0b5752069ce00d8ba","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.55,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":281,"end_line":null},"finding":"Load persisted state","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_state(path: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Load persisted state from disk.\"\"\"\n    p = Path(path)\n    if p.exists():\n        try:","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"db8dbe60b21a4e71397d99efe9b5bc585d8c92b9d99e52350c6f15fc85d3d6aa","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":281,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-5e019e4cf17c47cd8923e858eed7f997","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":298,"end_line":null},"finding":"Persist state to disk","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n\ndef save_state(state: dict, path: str):\n    \"\"\"Persist state to disk.\"\"\"\n    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(state, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"efc3f5b831a7b8907b45177178ec015ecdf49c42a1359c06d2c421bf513aee8d","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":298,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-2b0f5e9ce8344f7eba80c652159b626b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.79,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":81,"end_line":81},"finding":null,"explanation":"The parameter description specifies `--translate-to` with a default of `zh`, which indicates a built-in locale preference in the skill's natural-language behavior. The README does not frame this as an opt-in or justify the locale restriction as region-specific, so it can conflict with language-choice policy expectations.","remediation":"Document that translation language is user-selectable and avoid presenting Chinese as the assumed default without consent, or justify the locale default clearly as part of a region-specific use case.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":81,"end_line":81}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-5bcc70879c0a40c9be93b7b9b805fd05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":61,"end_line":61},"finding":null,"explanation":"The default configuration sets `translate_to` to `zh`, which hard-codes a specific locale preference in the skill's natural-language behavior. This can violate language/locale policy expectations when users have not explicitly chosen that language target.","remediation":"Remove the default forced locale, require the user to specify a target language when translation is enabled, or document and gate the language choice behind explicit user opt-in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/auto_mirror.py","start_line":61,"end_line":61}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-da48f9ba26a442c19a0c7ee62726bd1f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"